# macOS / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local dev
*.log
.cache/
.local/

# Test fixtures
test-*.html
*-copy.html
*-backup.html

# Build outputs (not used yet, but safe to ignore)
dist/
build/
*.min.css
*.min.js

# ...but vendor/ is checked-in third-party code, not a build output. Without this
# negation, *.min.js silently drops vendor/model-viewer.min.js from the commit:
# the site works in local preview (served from disk) and 404s in production, and
# the 3D model fails with no obvious cause. See vendor/README.md.
!vendor/**

# Video is hosted on Cloudflare R2, not in the repo.
# Cloudflare Workers rejects any asset over 25 MiB, so committing a
# reel here turns the deploy red. See media/README.md.
media/*.mp4
media/*.mov
media/*.webm

# Client deliverable viewers (tile pyramids) are hosted on Cloudflare R2 at
# media.parallaxaerial.uk -- NOT served by this Worker, and nothing in the
# site's HTML links to a local copy. One got committed by mistake on
# 2026-08-17 (97 MB, 9,130 files) and bloated .git's pack past Cloudflare
# Workers' 25 MiB per-asset limit, breaking every deploy until untracked
# 2026-08-20. See .assetsignore too -- belt and suspenders.
deliverables/
